---
source: crates/chain-syntax/tests/it/bad.rs
expression: "annotate(&text, &parsed.diagnostics)"
---
  1 | chain 2 "Types"
  2 | strip #1 "Lead"
  3 |   arp #2
  4 |   synth #3
  5 |   -- E213: the synth gives no MIDI to the arpeggiator after it
  6 |   arp #4
    |   ^ 6:3: error E213: `arp` takes midi at `notes`, and the inserts before it give audio
  7 | strip #5 "Room"
  8 | producer singer #6
  9 | producer pitch #7
 10 | -- E213: the camera of the avatar is a video, and the kick is audio
 11 | producer avatar #8 camera=@"Drums/Kick"
    |                    ^ 11:20: error E213: `camera` takes video, and @"Drums/Kick" gives audio
 12 | "Notes" -> #1
 13 | -- fine: a lane with lyrics into the singer
 14 | "Notes" -> #6
 15 | -- E213: the singer needs lyrics, and the chords have none
 16 | "Chords" -> #6
    | ^ 16:1: error E213: `#6` needs midi with lyrics=on, and "Chords" gives lyrics=off, and the host has no converter
 17 | -- fine: the host has a converter from stereo to mono
 18 | "Room" -> #7
 19 | -- E213: a strip takes audio or MIDI, not keyframes
 20 | "Keys" -> #5
    | ^ 20:1: error E213: `#5` takes audio or midi, and "Keys" gives keyframes
 21 | -- fine: a curve moves a parameter
 22 | "Volume" -> #5.gain
 23 | -- E213: audio cannot move a parameter
 24 | "Room" -> #5.pan
    | ^ 24:1: error E213: `#5.pan` is a parameter: it takes curve, and "Room" gives audio
 25 | #6 => "Sung"
 26 | -- E213: a lane of keyframes keeps no MIDI
 27 | #7 => "Keys"
    | ^ 27:1: error E213: "Keys" takes keyframes, and `#7` gives midi
